{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03007",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.09,
      "end_seconds": 2.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "welcome make yourself comfortable"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.74,
      "end_seconds": 4.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.14,
      "text": "Hi, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 6.21,
      "end_seconds": 10.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "morning, doctor i'll stay and fill in anything that's missed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.08,
      "end_seconds": 20.19,
      "duration_seconds": 8.11,
      "text": "so, that's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together. So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.04,
      "end_seconds": 30.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "yeah, um, it's flakes on my shoulders i thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.46,
      "end_seconds": 36.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "when was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.08,
      "end_seconds": 41.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Erm, around three weeks, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 42.13,
      "end_seconds": 45.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Hm, I'd say more like a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.79,
      "end_seconds": 51.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "okay, so roughly three to four weeks is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.68,
      "end_seconds": 53.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "that sounds about right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.88,
      "end_seconds": 58.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "how troublesome is it day to to day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.62,
      "end_seconds": 74.17,
      "duration_seconds": 14.55,
      "text": "It's severe, honestly. Um, and there's an itchy scalp as well, about two weeks now. Um, I've also had a little redness, since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.21,
      "end_seconds": 81.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "Have you had flakes on your shoulders before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.34,
      "end_seconds": 90.84,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last year, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.48,
      "end_seconds": 95.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "And what about hair loss, pain or pus?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.09,
      "end_seconds": 100.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.24,
      "end_seconds": 104.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "have you had rash elsewhere, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.31,
      "end_seconds": 108.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "No rash elsewhere, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.74,
      "end_seconds": 112.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Any trouble with the the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.24,
      "end_seconds": 115.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.94,
      "end_seconds": 121.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Right, what about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.23,
      "end_seconds": 126.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.46,
      "end_seconds": 130.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.8,
      "end_seconds": 134.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "I've got arthritis in my knees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.07,
      "end_seconds": 138.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Right, and anything else to add?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.39,
      "end_seconds": 148.26,
      "duration_seconds": 7.87,
      "text": "Yes, an underactive thyroid. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.01,
      "end_seconds": 149.94,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "I follow"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.94,
      "end_seconds": 158.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "Gout, for nearly five years. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.02,
      "end_seconds": 168.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.89,
      "text": "mm, okay right, so gout is already on your record we'll keep that in mind today"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.89,
      "end_seconds": 186.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.22,
      "end_seconds": 204.89,
      "duration_seconds": 16.67,
      "text": "Ah, uh, I take paracetamol, 650 milligrams, when needed for the knee pain. I take something called allo... allopurinol, 100 milligrams, maybe, once a day for the gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.8,
      "end_seconds": 213.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Have you got the box or the prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.72,
      "end_seconds": 219.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "let me think, no, it's at home"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.42,
      "end_seconds": 234.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.26,
      "end_seconds": 238.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "No, I've never reacted to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.76,
      "end_seconds": 244.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.81,
      "end_seconds": 258.93,
      "duration_seconds": 14.12,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.4,
      "end_seconds": 262.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.11,
      "end_seconds": 271.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.81,
      "end_seconds": 301.84,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 80 beats a minute, BP is 111 over 69, saturation 97 percent, temperature is 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.52,
      "end_seconds": 305.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Is that that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.81,
      "end_seconds": 314.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "We'll look at it it together shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.71,
      "end_seconds": 320.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.72,
      "end_seconds": 323.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "tell me if that's sore"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.14,
      "end_seconds": 341.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "there is fine greasy scaling across the scalp with no bald patches"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.14,
      "end_seconds": 358.43,
      "duration_seconds": 13.29,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Let me tell you where I've got to. I think we're dealing with simple dandruff at this stage. Seborrhoeic dermatitis is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.31,
      "end_seconds": 388.67,
      "duration_seconds": 18.36,
      "text": "For this, ketoconazole shampoo, 2%, twice a week, four weeks. It's for dandruff. Leave the shampoo on for five minutes before rinsing. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 393.41,
      "end_seconds": 394.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.7,
      "end_seconds": 400.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "see me again if not better in a month"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.06,
      "end_seconds": 406.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Ah, um, I'll note it in my calendar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 407.36,
      "end_seconds": 410.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "I think we're done unless you have questions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.31,
      "end_seconds": 414.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}